Jira auto-pickup disabled — do NOT poll Jira by label (battery/CPU).
Originally 2026-06-15 (battery drain); made permanent 2026-06-24.

This flag is the ONLY thing still off. As of 2026-06-26 the launchd timer
(com.conductor, every 300s) is intentionally back ON so it can do the *cheap*
work every tick:
  - PR/CI babysitting + marker-driven actions (conductor.sh, pre-pickup section)
  - worktree summaries (Pass 2: summarize-dirty -> summarize-worktree)
  - PR-state probing (Pass 3: probe-pr-state, throttled per session)

What this flag still does: conductor.sh sees it (line ~2453) and skips the Jira
label query + AI ticket picker — the actual battery culprit was the per-tick Jira
network poll, not the local summarize/babysit work. So the timer runs but never
auto-picks new tickets from Jira labels.

Manual dispatch still works: conductor run <project> "<ticket-url>"

To ALSO re-enable Jira label auto-pickup (the heavy part): delete this file.
To turn the whole timer back off:
  launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.conductor
  launchctl disable gui/$(id -u)/com.conductor
